WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.940
Around 1893 a family of Russian Jews fleeing

2
00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:08.160
persecution landed in New York with almost nothing.

3
00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:10.844
Their youngest son, a boy called Israel

4
00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:13.897
Baline, would grow up to write "God Bless America."

5
00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:17.922
Berlin took his oath as a United States citizen on

6
00:00:17.922 --> 00:00:21.596
6 February 1918, after several years of paperwork.

7
00:00:21.946 --> 00:00:24.175
Within months the new citizen was drafted.

8
00:00:24.525 --> 00:00:27.844
The singer Kate Smith introduced "God Bless America"

9
00:00:27.844 --> 00:00:31.226
on the radio on 11 November 1938, and Berlin assigned

10
00:00:31.226 --> 00:00:34.545
its royalties to a fund for the Boy and Girl Scouts.

11
00:00:34.895 --> 00:00:37.380
Four years later, in the film Holiday Inn, he

12
00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:40.306
introduced "White Christmas," which became one of the

13
00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:43.730
best-selling songs ever recorded and won him an Academy Award.

14
00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:47.389
Read the full story, with every source, on this page.
